@startuml
' Email claim intake: from an email arriving in claims@parasol.com to the email being filed.
' Keep in sync with docs/design/email-claim-intake.md (Workflow). Rendered by docs/render-diagrams.sh.
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F5F7FA
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF8E1
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

title Email claim intake workflow

|Customer|
start
:Emails claims@parasol.com;

|Intake system|
:Watcher receives the email (IMAP IDLE);
if (Auto-reply, self-sent, or a\nMessage-ID already processed?) then (yes)
  :No reply, no run;
else (no)
  :Record the Message-ID; move the email to processing;
  :Match the email to a claim (code, not the LLM):\nclaim number in subject or body, then reply headers;
  :Start one workflow run for the email\n(the watcher doesn't wait; a claim's emails\nrun in order, different claims in parallel);
  note right
    Everything below, apart from the claims
    processor's look-over, is that run's steps
    (including the wait and the decision).
  end note
  if (Claim matched, but the sender isn't\nthe claim's email address?) then (yes)
    :Reply: no matching claim\n(no details; write from the claim's\naddress or include the claim number);
  else (no)
    :Agents classify: new claim / follow-up / not a claim;
    note right
      The matched claim wins: an email matched to
      a claim is handled as a follow-up on it,
      whatever the classification says.
      Pending = Pending Information or Pending Review.
    end note
    if (Claim matched, in any other status\n(e.g. New, In Process, Processed, Denied)?) then (yes)
      :Reply: status answer\n(claim never updated);
    elseif (No claim matched,\nclassified not a claim?) then (yes)
      :Reply: not a claim;
    elseif (No claim matched,\nclassified follow-up?) then (yes)
      :Reply: no matching claim\n(no details; write from the claim's\naddress or include the claim number;\nnothing created or changed);
    else (claim matched and pending, or\nno claim matched, classified new claim)
      :Agents extract the details\n(over the whole correspondence);
      if (In code, before any claim is created or changed:\nnew claim whose policy number belongs to another customer?) then (yes)
        :Reply: policy inconsistency\n(no claim);
      else (no)
        :If the claim was waiting for review,\ncancel its waiting run;
        if (Every required detail present\n(incl. items the reviewer asked for)?) then (no)
          :Claim → Pending Information;
          :Reply: the missing details;
        else (yes)
          :Claim → Pending Review;
          :Reply: received, in final review;
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endif
endif
:File the email (processed folder);
note right
  The email is filed before the run waits or ends.
  If any step fails, before or after the wait, a failure
  listener moves it to the failed folder and the customer
  gets a "processing problem" reply.
end note
if (This run moved the claim\nto Pending Review?) then (no)
  stop
else (yes)
  :The run waits for the decision\n(no thread held; kept in PostgreSQL\nwhile the app runs);
  |Claims processor|
  :Later, separately: final completeness\nlook-over on the claim detail page\n(doesn't hold up the inbox);
  |Intake system|
  :The waiting run wakes with the decision\n(no LLM call);
  if (Decision?) then (Ready)
    :Claim → In Process;
    :Reply: thank you, we're working on your claim;
  else (Needs more information)
    :Claim → Pending Information;
    :Reply: exactly the items the processor ticked;
  endif
  stop
endif
@enduml
